Dear Daniel,

Another possible solution is to use the formula used for the procD.lm fits in morphol.disparity, to provoke the function to try to make the model fit, in situ, but I doubt this will work, either.

We are currently working aggressively to update geomorph and RRPP.  Part of this was imposed by the recent CRAN R version 4.4.0 update (not updated to 4.4.1), which has caused a flurry of other package updates.  For example, the Matrix library also updated and requires R >= 4.4.0, which is a dependency for RRPP and geomorph, but other packages do not require R >= 4.4.0, so there are some problems with syncing updates.  To make matters worse, we were in the process of making some internal updates — which do not change functions from the user perspective but work better — due to new functions (some introduced and some to be introduced).  Combined, these issues have forced package development to be both an active quest and high priority.  Hopefully we will have this sorted out within a few days.

Best,
Mike

